The save path for a new visit note runs through five layers. I read each one except the generic REST dispatch step in `DelegatingCrudResource`, which I did not open.

1. **Frontend form submit.** The form builds the payload and calls `saveVisitNote` for new notes, or `updateVisitNote` when editing (`openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes-form.component.tsx:406-437`).
2. **Frontend request function.** `saveVisitNote` POSTs the payload to `${restBaseUrl}/encounter` through `openmrsFetch` (`openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes.resource.ts:134-143`).
3. **Server REST entry point.** The generic `POST /{resource}` handler in `MainResourceController.create` resolves the `encounter` resource and calls `create` on it (`openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod-common/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/controller/MainResourceController.java:85-94`). The encounter resource's `save` is in `EncounterResource1_8` (`openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_8/EncounterResource1_8.java:185-191`). The 1.9 override is in `EncounterResource1_9`, which links provider back-references before calling `saveEncounter` (`openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/EncounterResource1_9.java:77-86`).
4. **Core service.** `EncounterServiceImpl.saveEncounter` enforces edit permissions, assigns a visit to new encounters, checks privileges, handles datetime and location changes on existing encounters, then calls the DAO (`openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/impl/EncounterServiceImpl.java:100-173`).
5. **Data access.** `HibernateEncounterDAO.saveEncounter` calls `HibernateUtil.saveOrUpdate` on the current Hibernate session (`openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/db/hibernate/HibernateEncounterDAO.java:79-82`). The actual SQL write happens when the session flushes, which I did not trace.

Uncertainty: the `create` → `save` hop inside `DelegatingCrudResource` was not read. The `onSubmit` function that wraps the form's save call was not identified by name.

